  "conclusion": "The required app-specific permission warm-up returned prompt-free inside its 10-second bound, performed zero input, and cleaned its transparent zero-operation process. The authorized mechanical issue #112 table repair was semantic-neutral, and every pre-target gate passed with the noncanonical fresh package excluded from target use. The unchanged controller launched the exact preserved candidate once, validated the candidate/session and zero-operation boundary, atomically published the marker, and entered the 120-second handoff. Direct coordinator marker validation passed. The single post-marker Computer Use read returned an authentication boundary in the under-1-second bucket because the Mac was locked and automatic unlock was unavailable. No app state was actionable, so no click or other Computer Use action occurred and no retry ran. The controller independently timed out after 1,705 observations without focus, cleaned its marker, and terminated the candidate before raise or observer execution. Terminal checks found the marker and publication temporary absent and zero TTRPG processes. No product operation, fixture, sampler, artifact, destination, dispatch, measurement, issue #95 operation, or issue #104 consumption occurred. Computer Use is retired for this M2 handoff; the one-real-owner-click route is the sole successor."
